---
name: Hello Domain 3
description: >
  The prompt feature 006 exercises the Foundry deployment with. It exists as a
  file rather than as a string inside call_model.py so that editing it is a
  diff and a commit — which is the whole of FR-006 and the only thing SC-003
  reads.
authors:
  - Valerio Quaranta
model:
  api: chat
  configuration:
    type: azure_openai
    # The endpoint is deliberately NOT written here. It contains
    # uniqueString(resourceGroup().id), so pinning it in a tracked file would
    # make the prompt stop working the first time the resource group is
    # rebuilt — and this feature's resource group is meant to be disposable.
    # call_model.py supplies it from AZURE_AI_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT at call time.
    azure_deployment: gpt-4.1-mini
  parameters:
    # Small on purpose. Every token here is real money at the rates in
    # docs/exam-notes/foundry-cost-model.md, and nothing about this feature's
    # objectives gets better with a longer answer.
    max_tokens: 200
    temperature: 0.2
sample:
  topic: the difference between a Standard and a Provisioned model deployment
---

system:
You are a concise assistant helping someone prepare for the Microsoft AI-300
exam. Answer in at most three sentences. Do not hedge and do not list
alternatives you are not recommending.

user:
Explain {{topic}}.
